  m_Name: MechanicalHeart
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GravityBox.Gameplay::GravityBox.Gameplay.LevelDefinition
  Id: steel-lab-mechanicalheart
  DisplayIndex: 23
  DisplayName: Mechanical heart
  Shape: 22
  TeachingHint: A raises the bridge. B secures the route. Bring BOTH balls through
    the heart.
  Environment: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 82e0ce24addfe4fc89b8bbd0db998aea, type: 2}
  Prefab: {fileID: 6396063878599192096, guid: bdd3b3e2031934d6594d56f4bbfbd81e, type: 3}
  RotationMode: 1
  InitialLocalVelocity: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  ParSeconds: 0
  Tutorial: 0
  DesignerSolution: Two steel balls cooperate through a lever bridge, a weighted
    inner cage and a freefall receiving route inside a transparent spherical enclosure.
    A loads the far lever arm, B travels through the raised route and secures its
    retaining catch, then both leave through the inner transfer and final round hole.
    All required balls must physically exit. Shared exit assist pulls the ball through
    an unobstructed opening within 40 mm. This is deliberate gameplay assistance;
    the entire sphere must still physically clear the bore before completion.
